  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "Acer platanoides 'Maltese Cross' Rare Norway Maple Zones 4-7 Acer platanoides ‘Maltese Cross’ is a broadleaf deciduous maple with green foliage and a rounded canopy, providing shade and seasonal interest. It thrives in full sun to dappled shade, tolerates drought once established, and adapts to a wide range of soils, including acidic, alkaline, clay, and well-drained types. This versatile tree is heat, humidity, pollution, and seaside/salt tolerant, making it suitable for urban and coastal landscapes. It attracts beneficial insects and birds, supports biodiversity, and is low-maintenance, reaching a 10 year height of 15-25 ft. Acer platanoides does not ship to CT, ME, MA, and NH."
  },
